            <td>Pinterest save functionality and Rich Pin validation</td>
            <td><a href="https://policy.pinterest.com/en/cookies" class="legal-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pinterest Cookie Policy</a></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>How to Control Cookies</h2>
      <p>You can control cookies through your browser settings. Most browsers allow you to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>View which cookies have been set</li>
        <li>Delete all or specific cookies</li>
        <li>Block third-party cookies</li>
        <li>Block all cookies (note: this will break some site functionality)</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Browser-specific instructions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647" class="legal-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chrome</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/clear-cookies-and-site-data-firefox" class="legal-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firefox</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/safari/manage-cookies-sfri11471/mac" class="legal-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Safari</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/view-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-a7d95376-f2cd-8e4a-25dc-1de753474879" class="legal-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Edge</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p>To opt out of Google Analytics tracking specifically, you can use the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" class="legal-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>.</p>

      <h2>Cookie Consent</h2>
      <p>When Google Analytics 4 is fully active on the site, we will implement a cookie consent mechanism that gives you control over analytics cookies before they are set. Essential cookies (required for the site to work) will still be used regardless of consent selection.</p>

      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this cookie policy when we add or remove third-party services. The "Last updated" date at the top reflects the most recent change.</p>

